{
  "_readme": [
    "GOLDEN PRICING CASES — docs/security/security-general.md §06, SEC-10.",
    "",
    "One file, two readers. packages/db/tests/pricing-golden.test.ts asserts it against",
    "app.price_slot (SQL); packages/core/src/pricing/rateRules.golden.test.ts asserts the",
    "SAME cases against resolveRateRule (TypeScript). The two implementations price every",
    "slot in the product — SQL when a booking is written, TS when the phone renders the",
    "grid — and a guest who is quoted one number and charged another is the failure this",
    "file exists to make impossible. Neither test owns the numbers; this file does.",
    "",
    "THE CASES ARE IN A FIXED PAST WEEK (Sun 2026-03-01 .. Sun 2026-03-08, Asia/Baghdad,",
    "UTC+3 with no DST). Fixed, so the expected values never move. Past, because",
    "app.price_slot is a pure function of (court, instant, duration) with no notion of",
    "'future' — and because every `validFrom`/`validTo` here confines these rules to that",
    "week, so inserting them cannot change the price of any slot another suite books.",
    "",
    "WHAT THE CASES COVER: both boundary minutes of every window (16:59/17:00,",
    "22:59/23:00, 08:59/09:00, 01:59/02:00); both sides of midnight on a weekday night and",
    "on a weekend night, including the day-shift that makes Saturday 01:00 the tail of",
    "FRIDAY (get it wrong and Friday night bills as a weekday); pricing by the SLOT START",
    "rather than its end; court-specificity beating a higher priority; a date-limited",
    "promotion; a winning-tier rule with no price for the requested duration falling",
    "through instead of black-holing the slot; a retired rule being ignored; and an",
    "unpriced duration resolving to nothing.",
    "",
    "expectedIqd null means NO rule prices the slot — app.price_slot returns zero rows and",
    "resolveRateRule returns null. The booking RPCs turn that into NO_RATE.",
    "",
    "GENERATED, then checked in. To change a case, change it here and make both tests green."
  ],
